      "id": "bd1d8851290db41bc8fe8a80c4817e9a8c5d98510e358717f1975c864fbd4412",
      "title": "CDC Steven M. Teutsch Prevention Effectiveness (PE) Fellowship 2027 (Paid)",
      "url": "https://opportunitydesk.org/2026/10/28/cdc-steven-m-teutsch-prevention-effectiveness-fellowship-2027",
      "category": "opportunities",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T20:31:28.952Z",
      "httpStatus": 200,
      "finalUrl": "https://opportunitydesk.org/2026/10/28/cdc-steven-m-teutsch-prevention-effectiveness-fellowship-2027/",
      "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
      "pageTitle": "CDC Steven M. Teutsch Prevention Effectiveness (PE) Fellowship 2027 (Paid) &#8211; Opportunity Desk",
      "pageDescription": "",
      "evidenceText": "CDC Steven M. Teutsch Prevention Effectiveness (PE) Fellowship 2027 (Paid) – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram CDC Steven M. Teutsch Prevention Effectiveness (PE) Fellowship 2027 (Paid) Jude Ogar October 28, 2026 3 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: January 8, 2027 Applications are open for the CDC Steven M. Teutsch Prevention Effectiveness (PE) Fellowship 2027 . CDC’s Steven M. Teutsch Prevention Effectiveness (PE) Fellowship is a two-year, post-doctoral, applied training fellowship. It addresses public health demand for quantitative policy analysis, health economics-based inquiry, integrative health services research, and rigorous decision modeling. The Traditional Track is offered for economists and health services researchers. The Analytics and Modeling Track is intended for disease modelers, ecologists, operations researchers, industrial engineers, and applied mathematicians. Since 1995, CDC has recruited and trained more than 300 effective decision scientists through the fellowship. With each new class, the PE Fellowship builds a cadre of scientists whose research provides vital information to decision makers. CDC, congress, and nongovernmental agencies use information on resource allocation to maximize the impact of public health programs. Benefits Fellows are paid at the General Schedule (GS) 12, step 3 level. They receive the same benefits as other federal employees, including medical insurance and leave. Fellows can be eligible for a salary increase after the first year of their fellowship, based on performance and written recommendation by appropriate management officials. Eligibility Applicants must hold a PhD (or equivalent) with all requirements completed before the start of the fellowship. All applicants with degrees obtained at non-US institutions may be asked to provide documentation of an academic credentialing evaluation to ensure degree requirements are equivalent on request. This demonstrates how the foreign degree equates to academic degrees issued in the United States. Additionally, degrees must be translated into English. Applicants must be in one of the following groups to be considered for the program. US citizens US Permanent Residents Non-United States citizens or US Permanent Residents eligible for one of the following visas/work authorizations: OPT STEM extension covering the entire two years of the fellowship (for current F1 visa-holders) TN visa authorized under the current United States-Mexico-Canada Agreement (USMCA) for eligible citizens of Canada and Mexico J1 cultural exchange visa (or J2 visa as spouse of J1-holder) H1B visa Other applicable visa that authorizes work in the US Non-US citizen candidates who advance in the selection process will be contacted to discuss their visa and work authorization. Eligible degrees include the following: Traditional Track Economics Agricultural economics Health services research Public health Other related quantitative field Analytics and Modeling Track Epidemiology Infectious disease modeling Disease ecology Applied mathematics Operations research or industrial engineering Biological science Data science Evolutionary or analytic biology Other related quantitative field Application The Class of 2027 fellowship application is open September 8, 2026, through January 8, 2027. Click here to apply For more information, visit CDC Steven M. Teutsch PE Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Aspen Strategy Group (ASG) Rising Leaders Program 2027 Next Article AI for Human Rights (AI4HR) Peer-learning Programme for Youth-focused Organisations 2027 Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
