      "evidenceText": "The Fix Research &amp; Advisory 50 organizations across 15 countries since 2019 Make better media decisions Research, consulting, and practical tools for independent media and the organizations behind them. Get in touch What we do The Fix started in 2019 as a small consulting team that couldn't find the industry research it needed — so we built it ourselves. Today it's both things: The Fix Research & Advisory, working with publishers, donors and implementing organizations across Europe and beyond, and The Fix Media, a trade publication read by a community of 3,000+ senior media professionals. Since then we've delivered 40+ consulting and research projects for 50+ media organizations and funders. We helped Hromadske nearly quadruple commercial revenue during a turnaround. We've trained 309 media managers from 20+ countries through the SSE Riga media management programs. Our sector studies with JX Fund, Thomson Reuters Foundation and others have been cited by The New York Times and the Reuters Institute. And when Russia launched its full-scale invasion, we co-led a campaign that raised around €3M for dozens of Ukrainian newsrooms. The sector we work in doesn't get calm years. Funding models break — USAID's shutdown was only the loudest recent case. Platforms rewrite the rules; audiences move. So we lead the transformation. Let's work on yours. 40+ consulting & research projects 50+ media organizations 309 managers trained · 20+ countries ≈€3M raised for Ukrainian newsrooms Services & products Research Understand your market before you bet on it — audience studies, benchmarking and sector intelligence for media organizations and funders. 12 published studies · cited by The New York Times and the Reuters Institute Explore Consultancy Turn strategy into results — business models, reader revenue, product and organizational development, from audit to implementation. 30+ successful projects since 2019 Explore Publishing Stay ahead of European media — reporting and analysis from The Fix Media, with new stories several times a week for 3,000+ senior media professionals. Want to reach them? Advertising & partnerships Explore Tech Two flagship tech products, already serving clients: AI Media Analytics — AI-supported assessment of media outlets at scale (content quality, framing, bias), validated by human experts; and Newstack — a SaaS service that helps media and NGOs save 50%+ on subscription costs. Put data and AI to work Explore Education Practice leadership under pressure — the Crisis Leadership Simulation and executive training, delivered in multiple languages. With SSE Riga · IPI · UN Women and many others Explore From The Fix — this month View All Monthly feature Inside the Iranian exile media sector Insights from an in-depth country profile prepared by JX Fund with support of The Fix Research and Advisory September 16, 2026 Read on The Fix September 2026 How OBCT built a transnational newsroom in Italy – and keeps it going 25 years later Read on The Fix August 2026 Survival school: How a modest program in Riga trained a generation of media managers from the post-Soviet space Read on The Fix August 2026 Why great podcasts struggle to grow and how to fix it, with Act3 Agency’s John Taylor Read on The Fix Meet the team Built by media practitioners TFRA brings together researchers, media strategists, product specialists, editors, and data experts working with independent media organizations across Europe and beyond. Jakub Parusinski Founder & Director View Profile Alesia Rudnik Head of Research View Profile Alex Vorobev Project Lead & Media Consultant View Profile Alina Afonchanka Project lead & media consultant View Profile Miraslau Chyhir Senior Associate, Data & Product View Profile Orsolya Seregély Senior associate & media consultant View Profile Rasel Ahmed Senior Analyst View Profile Anton Protsiuk Editor-in-Chief View Profile Anastasiia Kuzmenko Operations Editor View Profile Aizhan Kazakbaeva Project Lead & Media Consultant View Profile Jakub Parusinski Founder & Director View Profile Alesia Rudnik Head of Research View Profile Aizhan Kazakbaeva Project Lead & Media Consultant View Profile Alex Vorobev Project Lead & Media Consultant View Profile Alina Afonchanka Project lead & media consultant View Profile Miraslau Chyhir Senior Associate, Data & Product View Profile Orsolya Seregély Senior associate & media consultant View Profile Rasel Ahmed Senior Analyst View Profile Anton Protsiuk Editor-in-Chief View Profile Anastasiia Kuzmenko Operations Editor View Profile What partners say \"Organizing the first audience research and focus groups with BI readers is something BIRN needed, and that's where the Fix team perfectly fit the puzzle for us. They have experience in leading similar activities but also a significant amount of understanding for how independent media organizations often function - on limited resources and limited time but with great motivation and journalism skills.\" BI BIRN Balkan Insight Working with Alina and Jakub at The Fix has been a very valuable and effective experience for Radio Zamaneh. Their support helped us identify practical ways to improve and make parts of our digital work more efficient, particularly our English-language newsletter, Instagram presence, and other platforms. We truly appreciated their expertise, thoughtful guidance, and collaborative approach throughout the process. Thank you both for your support and contribution. It has been a valuable and memorable collaboration for us. Nasim Roshanaei Editor-in-chief, Persian & English Radio Zamaneh At the Anne-Marie and Gustaf Ander Centre for Media Studies at SSE Riga, our mission is to secure a sustainable future for independent journalism through education, specialized training, and cross-border collaboration. Read all Edgars Spuravs Director, SSE Riga Since 2022, JX Fund and The Fix have built a genuine research partnership around exile media — producing joint country profiles and landscape studies with a shared goal: to create a reliable evidence base that strengthens the exiled media ecosystem. The Fix brings a rare combination of editorial quality and practical field knowledge. Together we have created resources that are now widely used by funders, policymakers, and practitioners working in this space. Dina Khaskelberg Program manager, JX Fund \"Organizing the first audience research and focus groups with BI readers is something BIRN needed, and that's where the Fix team perfectly fit the puzzle for us. They have experience in leading similar activities but also a significant amount of understanding for how independent media organizations often function - on limited resources and limited time but with great motivation and journalism skills.\" BI BIRN Balkan Insight Working with Alina and Jakub at The Fix has been a very valuable and effective experience for Radio Zamaneh. Their support helped us identify practical ways to improve and make parts of our digital work more efficient, particularly our English-language newsletter, Instagram presence, and other platforms. We truly appreciated their expertise, thoughtful guidance, and collaborative approach throughout the process. Thank you both for your support and contribution. It has been a valuable and memorable collaboration for us. Nasim Roshanaei Editor-in-chief, Persian & English Radio Zamaneh At the Anne-Marie and Gustaf Ander Centre for Media Studies at SSE Riga, our mission is to secure a sustainable future for independent journalism through education, specialized training, and cross-border collaboration. Read all Edgars Spuravs Director, SSE Riga Since 2022, JX Fund and The Fix have built a genuine research partnership around exile media — producing joint country profiles and landscape studies with a shared goal: to create a reliable evidence base that strengthens the exiled media ecosystem. The Fix brings a rare combination of editorial quality and practical field knowledge. Together we have created resources that are now widely used by funders, policymakers, and practitioners working in this space. Dina Khaskelberg Program manager, JX Fund Why us Consulting discipline, built under constraint Our founding team trained at McKinsey and INSEAD — and ran newsrooms through revolutions, war and exile. That combination is the method: Western consulting rigor, plus the Eastern European habit of transforming under pressure, with small budgets and no stable ground. It's also why we work where most consultancies won't. Independent media in difficult markets is supposedly a sector without money. The 50+ organizations we've worked with — and results like Hromadske's near-4× revenue growth — suggest otherwise: the economics can work, if someone does the work. Clients & partners We bring solutions to make life easier for our customers. Request full pitchdeck Clients & partners We bring solutions to make life easier for our customers. Request full pitchdeck Let's work on your transformation Get in touch via form or email us - partnerships@thefix.media Click to copy email address Full Name * Looks good! Please enter your name. Email * Looks good! Please provide a valid email address. Your organization Looks good! Please enter your organization. Message * Looks good! Please enter your messsage. * These fields are required. LinkedIn · Email × At the Anne-Marie and Gustaf Ander Centre for Media Studies at SSE Riga, our mission is to secure a sustainable future for independent journalism through education, specialized training, and cross-border collaboration. We know that sustainable media businesses are vital for maintaining independent journalism and public accountability. Our collaboration with The Fix Team has been one of the pillars in delivering on this mission, allowing us to merge academic rigour with practical, modern industry insights. Together, we have collaborated closely on our Future Media Management projects - ranging from our four-week Mini-MBA for top media executives to intensive management training for mid-level leaders. Through these programs, we have successfully trained ~ 300 media managers from 20+ countries, equipping them to navigate an increasingly complex media ecosystem. A highlight of this partnership is the delivery of the Crisis Leadership Simulation, which provides newsroom leaders with hands-on, realistic practice in managing intense operational and strategic pressure. What makes The Fix team such an exceptional partner is that they are, first and foremost, media practitioners who understand the unique constraints and challenges independent outlets face today. They bring a rare combination of Western consulting discipline and real-world experience in running newsrooms under pressure. Edgars Spuravs Director of the Anne-Marie and Gustaf Ander Centre for Media Studies at SSE Riga; Member of the Advisory Board at Journalismfund Europe; Member of Media Policy Advisory Council at Ministry of the Culture of the Republic of Latvia.",
