      "evidenceText": "Green Global Fellowship 2027 for Emerging Leaders – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram Green Global Fellowship 2027 for Emerging Leaders Jude Ogar October 29, 2026 2 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: January 7, 2027 Applications are invited for the Green Global Fellowship 2027 . The Green Fellows Programme invites applications from emerging leaders committed to advancing sustainability through education, advocacy, and community action. The February 2027 cohort seeks changemakers from around the world who are ready to translate knowledge into meaningful, measurable impact. This is an action-oriented fellowship. Fellows are expected to apply what they learn, pass sustainability knowledge to younger generations, and demonstrate meaningful impact in schools and communities. Benefits Learn from sustainability experts and thought leaders. Develop leadership, advocacy, communication and project-management skills. Gain practical experience in sustainability education and community engagement. Connect with a network of young sustainability leaders. Receive a certificate upon successful completion of all fellowship requirements. Build a portfolio of documented sustainability projects and impact. US$1,000 Grand Prize (One fellow who fulfils all fellowship requirements and demonstrates documented impact may receive a US$1,000 post-fellowship award to support the continuation or expansion of the Educators Initiative. The award is conditional on full compliance with programme requirements and demonstrated results; selection alone does not guarantee funding.) Eligibility Be between 18 and 35 years old at the application deadline. Demonstrate a genuine commitment to sustainability and environmental action. Be committed to passing sustainability knowledge to the next generation through an Officially Green Club. Be available to attend all designated conferences and participate actively. Have reliable internet access and be prepared to document activities and impact. Application Completing the application form should take approximately 5–7 minutes. No prior professional experience in sustainability is required. They welcome applicants who are eager to learn, grow and make a difference.  Click here to apply For more information, visit Green Global Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Youth4Climate Services Innovation Hackathon 2026 Next Article Mozilla Foundation Fellowships 2027-2028 (up to $125,000) Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read 