      "title": "Mozilla Foundation Fellowships 2027-2028 (up to $125,000)",
      "url": "https://opportunitydesk.org/2026/10/29/mozilla-foundation-fellowships-2027-2028",
      "category": "opportunities",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T20:31:28.952Z",
      "httpStatus": 200,
      "finalUrl": "https://opportunitydesk.org/2026/10/29/mozilla-foundation-fellowships-2027-2028/",
      "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
      "pageTitle": "Mozilla Foundation Fellowships 2027-2028 (up to $125,000) &#8211; Opportunity Desk",
      "pageDescription": "",
      "evidenceText": "Mozilla Foundation Fellowships 2027-2028 (up to $125,000) – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram Mozilla Foundation Fellowships 2027-2028 (up to $125,000) Jude Ogar October 29, 2026 3 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: December 17, 2026 Applications are open for the Mozilla Foundation Fellowships 2027-2028 . Mozilla Foundation will award 10 Fellowships for the 2027–2028 period. They are looking for extraordinary individuals working at the edges of human imagination, on technology that’s too early, too unexpected, or too ambitious for anyone else to fund. Fellows are builders first, of tools and of the fields around them. But they are also defiant about who technology should serve, and rigorous about making it a reality. If that sounds like you, come build with Mozilla. Bring the wildest, most radical version of your idea: the one that questions who gets to decide and puts control back in the hands of the people who use it. Optimizing the status quo is somebody else’s job. Theirs is to build the alternatives. Fellowship Tracks The Fellowship has two tracks for builders at different stages of their careers. Both share the same commitment: developing Fellows into the kind of technology leaders a better technology future needs: Track I: Embedded Fellows – These Fellows are working on projects in collaboration with and backed by a civil society organization. Your host provides mentorship and a community to work inside. In return, you gain the experience of turning technical skill into community impact, and your host gains the expertise to advance its mission. Track II: Independent Fellows – Independent Fellows pursue their most ambitious idea in one of the areas above. You’ll turn your vision into products, working systems, and other innovations that advance better technology futures, with the freedom to choose the approach: a platform that proves an alternative model works, or tools that let other technologists build better systems. Benefits Track I: Embedded Fellows – $100,000 USD in total, as a $75,000 stipend and a $25,000 project budget. Track II: Independent Fellows – $125,000 USD in total, as a $100,000 stipend and a $25,000 project budget. Eligibility Mozilla Foundation funds projects that advance their charitable mission and create meaningful public benefit. In your application, they will ask you to describe the work you want to undertake, who stands to benefit, and what impacts you hope to see your work produce. You must be legally able to receive grant funds from Mozilla Foundation. They welcome builders from all walks and sectors to apply, and your work does not need to be focused on non-profits. They do require a charitable purpose, however. Applications must be submitted in English. Translation tools are welcome. They evaluate your ideas, not your language quality. Application Applications are reviewed through a multi-stage process. The primary review occurs at the Letter of Intent stage, with only a small number of shortlisted applicants invited to submit a full application in early 2027. Click here to submit the Letter of Intent For more information, visit Mozilla Foundation Fellowships . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Green Global Fellowship 2027 for Emerging Leaders Next Article The Interview Went Well. Why Is Your Old Boss Still Part of the Decision? Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
