      "pageDescription": "The Gordon N. Fisher / JHR Journalism Fellowship runs in tandem with the William Southam Journalism Fellowships. It offers one journalist from Sub-Saharan Africa or the Middle East a year of academic study at the University of Toronto.",
      "evidenceText": "The Gordon N. Fisher / Journalists for Human Rights Fellowship - GFMD « Back to all Fundings The Gordon N. Fisher / Journalists for Human Rights Fellowship Organisation: Journalists for Human Rights Status: Open Type: Fellowship Theme: Media support Funding Size: $4,900 per month Deadline: 01/12/2026 Eligibility: One journalist from Sub-Saharan Africa or the Middle East Target Region: Sub-Saharan Africa and the Middle East Application Language: English The Gordon N. Fisher / JHR Journalism Fellowship runs in tandem with the William Southam Journalism Fellowships. It offers one journalist from Sub-Saharan Africa or the Middle East a year of academic study at the University of Toronto. Eligibility The fellowship is offered to one journalist from Sub-Saharan Africa or the Middle East. Fellows must be proficient in spoken and written English, the language of instruction at the University of Toronto. The program carries no formal prerequisites and does not grant academic credit. As part of the immersive nature of the program, Fellows agree to refrain from professional work during the Fellowship and limit personal travel to official university holiday periods. Massey College encourages journalists from traditionally excluded and marginalized groups to apply. Do not use AI for your application How to Apply Applications opened on 01/10/2026 and close on 01/12/2026. Submit a professional biography, a current CV, a statement of intent, three samples of recent work produced in the last two years, and the names and contact information for two referees. Apply here . For more information, please visit this page . For the latest funding opportunities, profiles of media donors, and expert insight from GFMD’s MediaDev Fundraising Guide sign up for Bottom Line newsletter Sign Up Search Search for: This website uses cookies. By continuing to use the website you consent to the use and storage of cookies on your device. You are using an outdated browser which can 