      "evidenceText": "Middle East Eye Fellowship – Grants for Journalists Skip to content View Full List Grant details View all grants Middle East Eye Fellowship The Middle East Eye Fellowship is designed to support in-depth reporting by freelance journalists across the Middle East. The Fellowship program focuses each year on a theme of critical importance to the region, with applicants invited to submit detailed story pitches on the selected topic. Fellows will receive help turning their pitches into showpiece multimedia projects, while fostering broader connections within the newsroom. In 2026, Fellows explored the theme of water scarcity, with projects published from Ein al-Auja, Palestine ; Daraa, Syria, so far. The project theme for 2027 is the Rise of AI : Artificial intelligence is increasingly being used as a new tool in the machinery of oppression in the Middle East. From military targeting and securitization, to the spread of data centers, to disinformation campaigns and foreign meddling, the exploitation of AI technology is deepening inequalities and shattering lives across the region. Proof of residency will be required, with eligible countries listed on the application form; for two-person teams, at least one member must meet the residency requirements. This opportunity is reserved for freelancers and is not open to journalists in staff positions. Location Middle East Funding Type Fellowship Organization Middle East Eye Focus Area Subject Area Artificial Intelligence Award Size $1,500 Career Stage Editor's Note All freelance journalists based in the region are invited to apply. Deadline 11/01/2026 Apply Here",
