      "evidenceText": "Edward R. Murrow Press Fellowship – Grants for Journalists Skip to content View Full List Grant details View all grants Edward R. Murrow Press Fellowship Launched in 1949, the Edward R. Murrow Press Fellowship seeks to promote the quality of responsible and discerning journalism exemplified by the work of Edward R. Murrow. One Edward R. Murrow Press fellowship is awarded each year to a distinguished foreign correspondent or editor to spend 10 months full time in residence at CFR’s headquarters in New York. The fellow is expected to engage in sustained analysis and writing, expand their intellectual and professional horizons, and contribute to CFR’s active program of research, writing, and events 🌍 Applicants must have a firm grounding in and a proposal based on foreign policy or a global issue. Location New York Funding Type Fellowship Organization Council on Foreign Relations Focus Area Subject Area International Affairs Award Size $100,000 plus a modest travel grant Career Stage Applicants must have distinguished credentials in the field of journalism that includes covering international news as a working journalist for print, broadcast, or online media widely available in the United States. Editor's Note Must be a U.S. citizen for this residency in New York City Deadline 10/30/2026 Apply Here",
