      "pageDescription": "Calling all journalists passionate about youth mental health! SJN&#039;s HEAL and Youth Building and Belonging (YBB) Fellowships are here to support U.S. journalists reporting on, for, and with young people. Not sure which one&#039;s the right fit?",
      "evidenceText": "⭐ APPLY NOW: HEAL & Youth Building and Belonging Fellowships | Solutions Journalism Network Skip to main content Who We Are What Is Solutions Journalism? Respectful, Helpful & Fair Ethics Team Board of Directors Funders & Supporters Annual Reports & Financials Careers Impact Explore Our Impact How Solutions Journalism Rebalances the News Programs Climate Democracy Youth Mental Health Addressing Health Disparities Beacons Complicating the Narratives Educators Academies Student Media Challenge University Hubs Learning Lab Introduction to Solutions Journalism Webinar Toolkits & Guides Events & Opportunities Trainers All Resources Directory Solutions Story Tracker What You Can Do Sign Up for Newsletters Learn the Basics of Solutions Journalism Explore Our Programs See Upcoming Events & Opportunities Join the Directory Pitch Your Story Nominate Your Project for an Award Become an Accredited Trainer Teach Solutions Journalism Amplify Solutions in Your Community Events & Opportunities News Blog Solutions Insights Lab My Profile Donate Search Search Search Search Search Search Opportunity ⭐ APPLY NOW: HEAL & Youth Building and Belonging Fellowships Event Details Date October 16, 2026 Location Applicants must be based in the United States. Audience Journalists Learn More and Apply Now Calling all journalists passionate about youth mental health! SJN's HEAL and Youth Building and Belonging (YBB) Fellowships are here to support U.S. journalists reporting on, for, and with young people. Not sure which one's the right fit? Read through the application form for details , and join us for an info session on Sept. 28 to learn more! Related Content Event Info Session: HEAL & Youth Building and Belonging Fellowships September 28, 2026 Program Youth Mental Health Program Youth Building & Belonging Fellowship Program HEAL Fellowship Team Julia Hotz Fellowships Manager Upcoming Events Event Climate Peer Network Meeting November 12, 2026 Event Counterpart's Solutions Lab Training November 12, 2026 Event ⭐ APPLY NOW: Train-the-Trainers (December 2026 Cohort) November 15, 2026",
