      "finalUrl": "https://opportunitydesk.org/2026/11/03/mastercard-foundation-edtech-fellowship-uganda-cohort-2/",
      "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
      "pageTitle": "Mastercard Foundation EdTech Fellowship Uganda Cohort 2 &#8211; Opportunity Desk",
      "pageDescription": "",
      "evidenceText": "Mastercard Foundation EdTech Fellowship Uganda Cohort 2 – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram Mastercard Foundation EdTech Fellowship Uganda Cohort 2 Jude Ogar November 3, 2026 2 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: November 26, 2026 Applications are open for the Mastercard Foundation EdTech Fellowship Uganda Cohort 2 . The Mastercard Foundation EdTech Fellowship, Uganda, implemented by Hive Colab in partnership with the Mastercard Foundation, supports high-impact, growth-stage EdTech ventures to build sustainable and scalable education enterprises. The Fellowship strengthens ventures’ business models, improves the quality and relevance of their digital learning products, and expands access to quality, inclusive and learner-centred education. Selected ventures receive a catalytic milestone-based, equity-free grant, alongside a 12-month fellowship programme combining tailored business support, weekly mentorship and coaching, learning science and inclusive product design, market access, investment readiness and technical assistance. Ventures also receive up to 24 months of post-acceleration support focused on growth, market access, fundraising and long-term sustainability. Benefits Fellows receive catalytic funding, structured curriculum, one-on-one mentorship, partnership support, learning science guidance, and investor readiness advisory. Eligibility To apply, your venture must: Be locally founded and locally led, with leadership and decision-making rooted in Uganda Be at Early Revenue, Growth, or Scaling stage. Pre-revenue/idea-stage ventures are not eligible Deliver an inclusive learning solution; for example, one that reaches underserved learners such as youth, young girls, persons with disabilities, refugees, or rural/low-connectivity communities Be operating in Uganda, with the majority of learners/users based in Uganda Technology as the Core of Learning: Have an active EdTech platform where learning takes place. Ventures whose primary model is solely in-person or classroom-based learning are not eligible. Application Required documents: Certificate of incorporation (or equivalent registration document) Pitch deck Gender, Safeguarding, or Child Protection Policy (if you have one) Product Demo Video: a short demonstration of how your product works. Maximum 5 minutes. Please share a link (YouTube, Vimeo, or Google Drive) with viewing permission set to “anyone with the link” rather than uploading a file. Click here to apply For more information, visit Mastercard Foundation EdTech Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Pan-African Re/Insurance Journalism Awards 2027 Next Article L’Oréal-UNESCO for Women in Science US Program 2027 (up to $75,000) Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
